Q: Kestrel needs restarted when TLS certificate renewed A: <p>Kestrel doesn't need a restart for this. The certificate only gets pinned if you hand it over once at startup. Give Kestrel a selector callback instead and it asks you for the certificate per connection, so a renewed one is picked up on the next handshake:</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>builder.WebHost.ConfigureKestrel(kestrel =&gt;
{
    kestrel.ConfigureHttpsDefaults(https =&gt;
    {
        https.ServerCertificateSelector = (context, host) =&gt; _current;
    });
});
</code></pre>
<p>Keep <code>_current</code> in a holder that reloads the PEM when the file changes (a FileSystemWatcher, or re-read on a timer and compare the thumbprint). Don't read from disk inside the callback on every handshake; cache it and swap the reference only when the file actually changes.</p>
<p>If what you actually want is the whole thing automated (obtain and renew, not just reload), that's the ACME flow. I wrote a library for it, AutoHttps (disclosure: I'm the author), which does the selector wiring and the renewal:</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>builder.Services.AddAutoHttps(options =&gt;
{
    options.DomainNames.Add(&quot;example.com&quot;);
    options.EmailAddress = &quot;admin@example.com&quot;;
    options.AcceptTermsOfService = true;
});
</code></pre>
<p>It renews in place on the CA's schedule, so no restart and no cron job. Works with Let's Encrypt or any ACME CA: <a href="https://github.com/astralmaster/AutoHttps" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://github.com/astralmaster/AutoHttps</a></p>

Q: How to upgrade to com.android.tools.build:gradle:7.1.3 in Android Studio A: <p>Change your <strong>maven url</strong> from</p>
<pre><code>allprojects {
    repositories {
        google()
        mavenCentral()
        maven { 
            url 'https://jitpack.io' 
        }
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>to</p>
<pre><code>allprojects {
    repositories {
        google()
        mavenCentral()
        maven {
            url 'https://maven.google.com/'
            name 'Google'
        }
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>then press <strong>Sync Project</strong></p>
